WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.505
On first launch, keep the listening address at 127.0.0.1 and the port at
8787.

2
00:00:07.525 --> 00:00:10.930
This accepts connections from the same computer.

3
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.112
Choose a data directory, keep SQLite, and continue.

4
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:21.005
Choose an administrator username and password, then confirm the password.

5
00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:25.342
Leave the initial gateway key blank to generate one automatically.

6
00:00:25.362 --> 00:00:30.212
Skip the configuration import for a fresh installation, then finish setup.

7
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.968
Save the client address and gateway API key, then open the console.

8
00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:39.168
SillyTavern will use this gateway key.

9
00:00:39.188 --> 00:00:44.825
The provider login credential stays in GPROXY and is not entered into the
chat client.

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.230
Add a provider, choose OpenAI Codex, and name it codex.

11
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.955
Keep the official default address.

12
00:00:52.975 --> 00:00:57.405
If your network requires a proxy, select the system proxy.

13
00:00:57.425 --> 00:01:00.725
Save the provider and open its credentials.

14
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:06.455
Click Add by signing in, choose Browser authorization, and start sign-in.

15
00:01:06.475 --> 00:01:11.092
In Chrome, select your signed-in account and click Continue to confirm.

16
00:01:11.112 --> 00:01:15.318
After the redirect, copy the URL from the address bar.

17
00:01:15.338 --> 00:01:20.005
Return to GPROXY, paste the URL, and click Complete sign-in.

18
00:01:20.025 --> 00:01:23.062
The credential is saved automatically.

19
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.430
Check that the saved credential is enabled.

20
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.268
Click Test and select gpt-6.1-sol.

21
00:01:31.288 --> 00:01:38.275
A successful test with HTTP 200 confirms that the local GPROXY instance
can call Codex directly.

22
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.780
Create a model route named tutorial-codex.

23
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:45.680
Open its details and add a member.

24
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:51.255
Select codex as the provider and gpt-6.1-sol as the upstream model.

25
00:01:51.275 --> 00:01:54.430
Keep the default tier and weight, then save.

26
00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:57.362
Clients can now use this route name.

27
00:01:58.550 --> 00:02:01.768
Open API Connections in SillyTavern.

28
00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:05.730
Choose Chat Completion and Custom OpenAI compatible.

29
00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:14.738
Set the base URL to http, colon, double slash, 127.0.0.1, colon 8787,
slash v1.

30
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.868
Enter the local gateway key saved earlier, then connect.

31
00:02:19.888 --> 00:02:24.630
Load the model list, choose tutorial-codex, and keep streaming enabled.

32
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.275
Once the connection is valid, return to the chat.

33
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.568
Send a message asking for a short greeting in Chinese and English.

34
00:02:33.588 --> 00:02:37.043
The content shown here comes from a real request.

35
00:02:37.062 --> 00:02:42.400
The path is SillyTavern, the local GPROXY instance, and then Codex
directly.
